{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-29", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves (Status A, K-14, daylight 1/25 s), spectral sensitivity (E.N.D. 1.00) and normalised spectral dye densities digitised from the Kodak data sheet E-88 (KODACHROME 25, 64 and 200 Films, page 5; identical curves in E-55). Original data are property of Eastman Kodak Company. Dye density scale, density scale per channel, adaptation window and base density follow the conventions of the official spektrafilm slide profiles (Kodachrome 64 and the other slide films); the film base density is the Kodachrome 64 base shifted by the minimum-density difference of the two sheets. Curve position set so that equal normalised dye amounts (visual neutral) fall on mid-grey. Derived from spektrafilm profile format; modified by graineo.", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; spektrafilm profile format and wavelength grid, and conventions (dye density scale, density scale, adaptation window, base density) taken from official spektrafilm slide profiles."}, "info": {"stock": "kodak_kodachrome_25", "name": "Kodak Kodachrome 25", "type": "positive", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "weak", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "color", "densitometer": "status_A", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 0.2, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "grain_scale": 0.668, "card": {"maker": "Kodak", "iso": 25, "type": "Farbumkehrfilm (Dia)", "rms": 9, "additional": "MTF 50 % bei etwa 44 lp/mm (Datenblatt)", "text": "Der feinkörnigste und schärfste Kodachrome: tiefe Schwarztöne, kräftiger Kontrast und satte, warme Rottöne, der klassische Dia-Look aus Reise- und Naturfotografie. Er verzeiht kaum Belichtungsfehler, Lichter brennen schnell aus und Schatten laufen dicht zu.", "source": "Kodak E-88", "process": "K-14 (die Farbstoffe entstehen erst bei der Entwicklung)", "period": "eingeführt 1974", "suitable": ["Landschaft und Natur bei Sonne", "Dia-Projektion", "feine Details"], "less_suitable": ["schwaches Licht (ISO 25)", "kontrastreiche Motive ohne Reserve"], "tips": ["Diafilm: kein Papier. Die Filmbelichtung ist entscheidend; Lichter lassen sich nicht retten.", "Der Filmlook „Kodachrome · klassisch“ nutzt Kodachrome 64, die Einstellungen lassen sich auf den 25er übertragen."], "facts": [{"text": "Kodachrome 25 und 64 ersetzten 1974 mit dem neuen K-14-Prozess die früheren Kodachrome II und X.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kodachrome"}, {"text": "Das Datenblatt E-88 von 2002 führt Kodachrome 25, 64 und 200 gemeinsam auf; die Fassung von 2009 kennt nur noch 64 und 200.", "source": "Kodak E-88 (März 2002 und Juni 2009)"}]}}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725.0, 730.0, 735.0, 740.0, 745.0, 750